// EXPECT-DIAG: E131
// EXPECT-DIAG: No such method!
// Regression test: calling a method on a non-struct value (int, string,
// pointer-to-non-struct) must be a clean compile error.
//
// Before this fix, TypeChecker::visitMethodCall()'s fallback ("be
// permissive") left the call unresolved with zero diagnostic, and the pre-
// pass's body codegen (src/main.cpp, sub-pass 3b) ran anyway regardless of
// whether the pre-pass TypeChecker had found any errors -- reaching
// Codegen's `llvm::report_fatal_error("Internal error: method call on
// unsupported type. This is a compiler bug.")` and ABORTING THE WHOLE
// COMPILER PROCESS (SIGABRT), before the main-pass TypeChecker (which
// correctly gates its own codegen) ever got a chance to run and print a
// real diagnostic. Fixed by (a) TypeChecker raising a real error for this
// case, and (b) gating the pre-pass's body-codegen sub-pass on the
// pre-pass TypeChecker actually being clean (see PreTCClean in main.cpp).

fn main(): int {
    mut x: int = 5;
    x.foo();
    return 0;
}
